# The non-secret settings of the collector. The prod overlay generates the
# ConfigMap tally-openstack-collector from this file, and the collector reads
# every key of it as an environment variable.
#
# The file takes any non-secret TALLY_OSC_* variable, one KEY=VALUE per line:
# no export, no quoting. docs/reference/configuration/tally-openstack-collector.md
# lists them with their defaults. TALLY_OSC_EXCHANGES and TALLY_OSC_QUEUE_TYPE
# are the two a deployment usually sets.
#
# Six variables are fixed by the openstack-collector component, and a line for
# one of them here changes nothing: TALLY_OSC_HTTP_PORT,
# TALLY_OSC_AMQP_URL_FILE, TALLY_OSC_TOKEN_FILE, TALLY_OSC_REPORTING_URL,
# TALLY_OSC_REPORTING_INSECURE and TALLY_OSC_BUFFER_PATH. The broker URL and
# the ingest token are Secrets and belong in no line of this file.

# Required. The cloud every emitted event is attributed to, which is the cloud
# the ingest credential is issued for. It ships empty, because a guessed cloud
# books usage to the wrong one, and `make prod-up` refuses to run until it is
# set.
TALLY_OSC_CLOUD=
